+/*  ChopGimp: "fast preview" rendering.
+ *
+ *  The projection is rendered in idle callbacks on the main thread.  While
+ *  one rendering iteration runs, no input event is processed and the
+ *  pointer cannot move.  GIMP's chunk iterator spends up to 1/15 s per
+ *  iteration, which makes the pointer stutter when the image has heavy
+ *  filters (layer effects) on a big canvas.
+ *
+ *  With fast preview (enabled by the display for image projections):
+ *
+ *  - while the user acts on the image (input events on the canvas, or the
+ *    image being updated repeatedly), an iteration is limited to a few
+ *    milliseconds, so input events and canvas redraws, which have a higher
+ *    priority than the projection idle, run at every frame.  GEGL still
+ *    processes each chunk with all its worker threads;
+ *
+ *  - while the image keeps being updated, only the displayed part of the
+ *    image (the priority rect) is rendered; the rest is deferred until the
+ *    updates stop for CHOPGIMP_PROJECTION_SETTLE_TIME.
+ *
